  "review_note": "Reviewed Docker recovery resource evidence at 2990d411feb71ba45fb0e64111266bda2694469b. All 982 distinct selected tests pass against 1,791 frozen Rust/Cargo/config inputs with retained executable/result hashes. Eight adapter cases, two real Engine cases and one native rooted binding/provider-interface case verify memory accounting, immutable evidence, changed-limit/start refusal and Ready/Active resource integration. The default VM correctly exposes a lower effective limit than a configured 3-GiB container; its evidence is refused, while a separate 256-MiB container proves positive sampling. Disk/copy/worker bounds remain explicitly deployment-enforced. Full managed startup, combined five-node RustFS extent recovery with foreground writes, departure/return evidence, multi-failure/rolling policy, desired capacity/resize, full CI, density, TPS/p99 and soak remain open. Raw evidence stays outside the PR and the goal remains active."
